# Hubei_KENTO_Elec_KT_0603B — component wrapper: local KiCad symbol + footprint, LCSC pinned
# in properties (feeds the JLC BOM/CPL fields).
#
# KT-0603B: 0603 blue indicator LED (peak 463-469nm / dominant 460-475nm). Canonical BLUE
# indicator per CLAUDE.md's 2026-07-26 LED-family pinning — MCU/comms status. JLCPCB Extended;
# LCSC stock 309,050 pcs 2026-07-26 (well above the low-hundreds-of-boards bar). Datasheet
# (KENTO, C2288): IV 70-175mcd min-max @ IF=5mA; VF 2.6-3.1V min-max @ IF=5mA (no typ column —
# VF_max=3.1V is this wrapper's conservative/high sizing estimate). Same footprint envelope
# (0.8x0.8mm pads at +-0.75mm, 0603 body) as the rest of the KT-0603 family and the retiring
# KT-0603YG, so swapping colours needs no layout-script position changes.
#
# 3V3-headroom note (CLAUDE.md standing rule, same as KT-0603G): at VF_max=3.1V, a 3.3V rail
# leaves only ~0.2V across the series R. Where this LED taps 3V3 directly, size R against VF_MIN
# (worst case for current), accept it running dim at the VF_max bin, and bench-trim R if needed.

A = io("A", Net, optional = True)
K = io("K", Net, optional = True)

Component(
    name = "Hubei_KENTO_Elec_KT_0603B",
    footprint = File("Hubei_KENTO_Elec_KT_0603B/LED0603-RD_C2288.kicad_mod"),
    symbol = Symbol("Hubei_KENTO_Elec_KT_0603B/KT-0603B_C2288.kicad_sym"),
    prefix = "D",
    part = Part(mpn = "KT-0603B", manufacturer = "Hubei KENTO Elec"),
    properties = {"LCSC": "C2288", "MPN": "KT-0603B"},
    pins = {
        "A": A,
        "K": K,
    },
)
